    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0053" n="807" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg807"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/3551</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-30T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 30, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6122. My 5958, April 7, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d8-f1"/> Order in council
                    dated 27th instant publishes withdrawal of statutory black list and I am
                    informed this morning by Lord
                        Robert Cecil that British Government has withdrawn the
                    confidential black lists so far as they relate to firms in the United States,
                    Philippines and Porto Rico.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
